# Modal stack authoring

Package layers (import from the subpath, never from `src/` or `lib/`):

| Subpath | Contents |
|---|---|
| `@slavayakimov/react-native-modal-stack/core` | `ModalController` (stack: `push`, `replace`, `pop`, `close`, `dismiss`, `openAfterClose`), no React |
| `.../react` | `createModalRegistry`, `configureModals`, `ModalProvider`, `useModalDraft`, `toggleDraftId`, `useModalDismissHandler` |
| `.../react-native` | `createSheetShell`, `FitBox`/`ContentBox`/`BareBox`, `FooterContent`, `FooterHeight`, `SheetHeaderBar`, `useKeyboardGeometry` |
| `.../navigation` | `reactNavigationScreen` adapter |
| `.../kit` | `KitSheetShell`, `ModalKitProvider`, `ActionMenuSheet`, `ConfirmSheet`, `OptionListSheet`, `CheckboxListSheet` |

## Registry

- `createModalRegistry<Ctx>("namespace")` — the namespace is unique per app (camelCase feature name). Runtime key is `namespace/key`, so keys inside a registry stay short (`actions`, `deleteConfirm`). A duplicate namespace with different keys logs `[modal-stack]` in dev.
- Payload is declared with `m.def<P>({...})`; steps without payload use `m.def({...})`. `open("key")` without a required payload does not compile — that is the check. Never cast `payload` with `as`.
- One `Portal` per registry per screen. Mount it as a sibling of the screen content, not inside a `ScrollView`.
- `title` is passed through `translate` from `configureModals` (identity by default). Put the title in the registry **or** render `SheetHeaderBar`/`KitHeader` in the body — never both.
- Pushed steps (anything reached with `push`) take their title from the registry, so the shell renders the back arrow and the title on one row.

| Scenario | `layout` | Title | Footer |
|---|---|---|---|
| Menu, confirm, option list | `fit` | registry or kit `title` prop | kit sheets handle it; custom body → `FooterContent` |
| `fit` + `TextInput` | `fit` | registry | `FooterContent` wrapping the buttons (required) |
| Long form, address search | `form` | body | `FooterHeight` or `FooterContent includeKeyboard={false}` |
| Long list with own styles | `scroll` | registry | own padding |
| Pagination inside `fit` | `fit` | body | `useFitScrollNearEnd(fetchNext)` |

## Data

- Long-lived data (lists, handlers, `isPending`, selected id) → `Portal` props, read as `ctx` in `render`.
- One-off data for a step (target id, mode) → payload: `open(name, payload)` / `push(name, payload)`, read as `payload`.
- Async: the mutation lives on the screen or in the body; `isPending` → `disabled` + `isLoading`; close in `onSuccess`, not before the response. With `useModalDraft` and async commit pass `onClose: () => undefined`.
- Callbacks in a payload must be one-shot. Repeatable handlers go into `ctx`.

## Navigation

| Need | API |
|---|---|
| Open the first step / replace the current one | `open(name, payload)` |
| Go to a nested step with Back | `push(name, payload)` |
| Back | `nav.back()`; a cancel button in a body: `nav.canGoBack ? nav.back : nav.close` |
| Close everything after commit | `nav.close()` or `close()` from `useModal()` |
| Jump to **another** registry, or race with the keyboard | `openAfterClose(name, payload)` |
| From non-React code | `getDefaultModalController().push(XxxModals.request("key", payload))` |

Swipe and backdrop call `controller.dismiss()`: depth > 1 pops, otherwise closes. To intercept (sub-view inside one step, busy state) use `useModalDismissHandler(handler, enabled)`; returning `true` keeps the sheet.

Forbidden: `openAfterClose` inside one registry, `close()` on Back at depth > 1, `Keyboard.addListener` in modal bodies, fixed `paddingBottom` for the keyboard, deep imports.

## Keyboard

Read geometry only through `useKeyboardGeometry()` / `KeyboardGeometryStore`.
`fit` — the shell does not lift; `FooterContent` (default `includeKeyboard`) grows the sheet. `form`/`scroll` — the shell lifts itself; `FooterContent includeKeyboard` there doubles the offset.

## Kit sheets

- `configureModals({ Shell: KitSheetShell })` once at app start; wrap the app in `ModalKitProvider theme={...}` for colours, radius, font sizes and default labels (`select`, `cancel`, `confirm`, `empty`).
- `ActionMenuSheet` items push the next step; `ConfirmSheet` gets `onCancel = nav.canGoBack ? nav.back : nav.close`; `OptionListSheet` closes in `onSelect`; `CheckboxListSheet` with `initialSelectedIds` keeps a draft and closes the stack on confirm, with `selectedIds` it is controlled.
- When the app has its own design system, build sheets with the same props shape and keep the kit only as a reference.

## Template

```tsx
import { createModalRegistry } from "@slavayakimov/react-native-modal-stack/react";
import { ActionMenuSheet, ConfirmSheet } from "@slavayakimov/react-native-modal-stack/kit";

type Ctx = { onDelete: (id: string) => void; isDeleting: boolean };
type Target = { id: string };

const m = createModalRegistry<Ctx>("tasks");

export const TaskModals = m.build({
    actions: m.def<Target>({
        layout: "fit",
        render: ({ payload }) => <Actions target={payload} />,
    }),
    deleteConfirm: m.def<Target>({
        layout: "fit",
        title: "Delete task?",
        render: ({ ctx, payload, nav }) => (
            <ConfirmSheet
                destructive
                confirmLabel="Delete"
                isLoading={ctx.isDeleting}
                onCancel={nav.canGoBack ? nav.back : nav.close}
                onConfirm={() => ctx.onDelete(payload.id)}
            />
        ),
    }),
});

function Actions({ target }: { target: Target }) {
    const { push } = TaskModals.useModal();
    return (
        <ActionMenuSheet
            items={[{ key: "delete", label: "Delete", destructive: true, onPress: () => push("deleteConfirm", target) }]}
        />
    );
}
```

Screen: `const { open } = TaskModals.useModal();` → `open("actions", { id })`, and `<TaskModals.Portal onDelete={...} isDeleting={...} />` next to the list.

## Checklist

- [ ] `createModalRegistry` with a unique namespace; payload declared in `m.def<P>`, no `as`.
- [ ] One `Portal` per registry per screen, outside `ScrollView`.
- [ ] Title in the registry or in the body, not both; pushed steps use the registry title.
- [ ] `layout` and footer follow the table; `fit` + `TextInput` → `FooterContent`.
- [ ] Nested steps use `push`, Back uses `nav.back`; `openAfterClose` only across registries.
- [ ] Async: `isPending` → `disabled` + `isLoading`; close in `onSuccess`.
- [ ] Smoke: open → nested step → back → swipe → leave the screen (no sheet left over the next screen).
